# MintBot — Agent Instructions & Executive Project Summary

> **AGENT DIRECTIVE & EXECUTIVE MEMORY**
> This file is read by AI agents working on MintBot. Maintain all invariants, constraints, and update `CONTEXT.md` on every feature change.

---

## 1. Project Mission & Technology Stack
- **Target Network:** Robinhood Chain (Arbitrum Orbit L2, Chain ID `4663`)
- **RPC / WSS:** `https://rpc.mainnet.chain.robinhood.com` | `wss://rpc.mainnet.chain.robinhood.com`
- **Core Stack:** TypeScript, Node.js (v18+), Viem, Express, WebSocket (`ws`)
- **Dashboard:** Standalone Vanilla HTML/CSS/JS (Neobrutalist Emerald Green theme `#10B981`, Lucide icons, Inter + JetBrains Mono)
- **Port:** `http://localhost:3000` (`npm run ui`)

---

## 2. Critical Protocol Invariants (MUST FOLLOW)

1. **OpenSea SeaDrop Drops:**
   - Canonical SeaDrop Router: `0x00005EA00Ac477B1030CE78506496e8C2dE24bf5`
   - OpenSea Fee Recipient: `0x0000a26b00c1f0df003000390027140000faa719`
   - When a contract implements `mintSeaDrop(address,uint256)`, **NEVER** call the NFT contract directly — route through the SeaDrop router via `mintPublic(nftContract, feeRecipient, zeroAddress, quantity)`.

2. **On-Chain Auto Price Detection:**
   - Query `getPublicDrop(nftContract)` on the SeaDrop router (`0x00005EA00Ac477B1030CE78506496e8C2dE24bf5`) to retrieve exact `mintPrice`, `startTime`, `endTime`, and `maxTotalMintableByWallet`.
   - Never hardcode prices or assume `0 ETH` without probing on-chain first.

3. **Pre-Signed T-0 Byte Blast for Scheduled Mints:**
   - At `T - 5s`: Pre-fetch nonces and pre-sign raw EIP-1559 transaction hex (`wallet.client.signTransaction(...)`) into memory.
   - At `T - 0s`: Immediately broadcast pre-signed raw bytes via `publicClient.sendRawTransaction(...)` across all wallets in parallel.

4. **Multi-Wallet Filtering:**
   - All strategies and session handlers must respect `selectedWallets` (`walletIndices`) so users only fire the specific wallets checked in the UI.

5. **BigInt Serialization:**
   - Express cannot serialize raw JavaScript `BigInt`. Always convert BigInts to strings (`toString()`) in `/api/*` responses.

6. **Living Documentation:**
   - Whenever any feature, strategy, contract address, UI control, or parameter is added or updated, **ALWAYS update [`CONTEXT.md`](file:///C:/Users/Tyrone%20James%20Bacolod/orca/projects/mintingBot/CONTEXT.md)**.

